THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE

Folio bundles open-source libraries under their own licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0,
ISC, BSD), among them Electron, CodeMirror, TipTap, markdown-it, Mermaid,
KaTeX, highlight.js, pptxgenjs, JSZip, hot-formula-parser, dagre and the Model
Context Protocol SDK; Folio Sheets adds Univer (Apache-2.0), Apache ECharts
(Apache-2.0), Arquero (BSD-3-Clause), SheetJS Community Edition (Apache-2.0),
xlsx-kit (MIT), quickjs-emscripten (MIT), node-forge (BSD-3-Clause, chosen from
its BSD-3-Clause or GPL-2.0 dual license), PivotTable.js (MIT), React (MIT),
RxJS (Apache-2.0) and json-diff-ts (MIT). Their notices are kept in
node_modules and in the built application's license files.

OPTIONAL COMPONENTS (downloaded only when the person turns on a feature)

The meeting recorder downloads, from pinned addresses checked by SHA-256, parts
that are not included in Folio and keep their own licenses, listed in
Settings → Optional features and in src/main/features/catalog.js:
  - sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0), Xiaomi Corporation and contributors
  - Silero VAD (MIT), Silero Team
  - Whisper large-v3-turbo (MIT), OpenAI; converted to ONNX int8 by sherpa-onnx
  - Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3 (CC-BY-4.0), NVIDIA; converted to ONNX int8 by sherpa-onnx
  - llama.cpp (MIT), the ggml authors
  - Qwen3-1.7B (Apache-2.0), Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud; GGUF by Unsloth

Folio Sheets downloads the same way, when the person turns them on:
  - DuckDB (MIT), DuckDB Foundation
  - Pyodide (MPL-2.0) and its Python packages under their own licenses
